1
00:00:00,799 --> 00:00:04,299
BFS Test Data Filler – a Chrome extension that fills banking forms with synthetic test data

2
00:00:04,299 --> 00:00:05,632
Open the side panel from the toolbar icon (or the welcome page)

3
00:00:05,632 --> 00:00:10,458
On the credit card form it finds 21 fields and works out what each one expects

4
00:00:10,458 --> 00:00:12,961
A seed makes the data reproducible – seed 1083 gives the same applicant every time

5
00:00:12,961 --> 00:00:17,874
Valid profile: one consistent synthetic applicant, highlighted in green

6
00:00:17,874 --> 00:00:22,746
Submit – the application accepts every value

7
00:00:22,746 --> 00:00:25,813
Negative test: make only the SSN invalid – everything else stays valid

8
00:00:25,813 --> 00:00:29,995
The note says which rule it breaks: area 666 is never issued

9
00:00:29,995 --> 00:00:33,197
The app rejects it with exactly one field error – as it should

10
00:00:33,197 --> 00:00:37,674
Next invalid SSN: 078-05-1120, the 1938 "wallet" number that was publicly voided

11
00:00:37,674 --> 00:00:41,674
Finding: the app approves an application with a voided SSN – log a defect

12
00:00:41,674 --> 00:00:49,246
Boundary profile: valid edge cases – turns 18 today, credit score 300 or 850, ZIP 00501…

13
00:00:49,246 --> 00:00:56,000
Region India: PAN, Aadhaar (Verhoeff check), IFSC, GSTIN (check character), UPI, PIN code

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,265
Region UK/EU: IBAN (mod-97), sort code, NI number – including fields in an iframe and a web component

15
00:01:04,265 --> 00:01:10,278
Generate tab: values for API tests – every invalid value says why it is invalid

16
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:15,285
Runs locally: no network access, nothing collected. Copy the data as JSON or Markdown for your evidence.
